.IX Title "GPGLIST 1"
.TH GPGLIST 1 2024-07-13 "perl v5.38.2" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
gpglist \-\- show who signed which of your UIDs
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.IP "\fBgpglist\fR [\fB\-\-signer=\fR\fIkeyid\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-revoked\fR] \fIkeyid\fR" 4
.IX Item "gpglist [--signer=keyid] [--show-revoked] keyid"
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBgpglist\fR takes a keyid and creates a listing showing who signed \fIkeyid\fR's user IDs.
.PP
.Vb 7
\&        $ gpglist 6D8ABE71
\&        +\-\-\-\-\-  1 Christoph Berg <cb@df7cb.de>
\&        |  +\-\-  2 Christoph Berg <cb@cs.uni\-sb.de>
\&        1  2  
\&        x     7929AB90F7AC3AF0 Martin Helas <mhelas@helas.net>
\&        x  x  29BE5D2268FD549F Martin Michlmayr <tbm@cyrius.com>
\&           x  7DDB2B8DB4B462C5 Martin Wanke <mawan@mawan.de>
.Ve
.PP
By default only non-revoked identities are listed, but it can be
overridden it with \fB\-\-show\-revoked\fR.
.PP
One or more \fB\-\-signer\fR option can be used to limit signers to the
matching keys.  See the GnuPG manual for the different ways to specify a
key or user ID.
.PP
The path to the gpg binary can be specified with the \fIGNUPGBIN\fR
environment variable (default: \f(CW\*(C`gpg\*(C'\fR).
.SH "نویسندگان (AUTHORS)"
.IX Header "AUTHORS"
.IP "Uli Martens <uli@youam.net>" 4
.IX Item "Uli Martens <uli@youam.net>"
.PD 0
.IP "Peter Palfrader <peter@palfrader.org>" 4
.IX Item "Peter Palfrader <peter@palfrader.org>"
.PD
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
